<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vikramaditya VI</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1076–1126</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vikramaditya VI was the most celebrated ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-chalukya-empire">Western Chalukya Empire</a> of Kalyani. During a fifty-year reign he founded the Chalukya Vikrama era, held off the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Cholas</a> and patronised scholars, among them the poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bilhana">Bilhana</a>, who wrote his biography, and the jurist Vijnaneshwara, author of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mitakshara">Mitakshara</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vikramaditya-vi.jpg" alt="Vikramaditya VI" width="320" height="451" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: B. Lewis Rice (Benjamin Lewis Rice, 1837-1927) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Old_Kannada_inscription_(1077_AD)_of_Kalyani_Chalukya_King_Tribhuvanamalla_Vikramaditya_VI_in_Panchabasti_temple_at_Humcha.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
